========================================================================
SOURCE (7.1 walker — live)
========================================================================

```
pub fn c_guard_scan_idents(env, sink, args)
  linear while i < chars_len(args)
  skip "..." (escape-aware), // line, /* */ block
  ident start = _/alpha; cont = alnum/_
  let name = str_slice(args, start, i);   // ONE slice, not concat
  c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved(env, sink, name)
```

Grep inside the function body:

| Pattern | Hits |
|---------|------|
| `name = name + c` | **0** |
| `name = name +` | **0** |
| `out = out +` | **0** |
| `ident = ident +` | **0** |
| `str_slice(args, start, i)` | **1** |

Classification still uses `char_at` (1-char `OoStr` per visit). That is
the language floor, not quadratic ident accumulate. Domain A
(`s71_domain_a.oot`) already named this.

**7.10** remains `c_parse_secret_env` (`c_emit_secret.oo:60`)
`name = name + c` — **different function**.

